1786554989662063	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy7hU		item.assign	bn-p3m9	{"action":"assign","agent":"maw-dev"}	blake3:p9bxl_Agz0PZetdmpj18bp0UTjxkusuYfwTAy0Egavw
1786555741183486	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy7xU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"ROOT CAUSE FOUND + REPRODUCED (deterministic, no concurrency needed). The field-report premise was wrong: bn-3huh7/bn-16v3x were NOT freshly created at 20:23-20:26. Recovered oplog blobs from continuum (git fsck --unreachable) prove: create bn-3huh7 20:01:03.388 epoch=44cff63; create bn-16v3x 20:01:23.482 epoch=44cff63; both auto-rebased 20:09:28 44cff63 -> 96a1fe7 (trigger auto-rebase:merge(bn-37o0d)); then NO oplog entry until 20:55. So both sat at 96a1fe7 while epoch/current moved to 613d8fa (maw epoch sync at 20:15, which does not touch workspaces) and trunk moved to ea85bf6.\n\nMECHANISM: merge.rs reconcile_ff_absorb. ff_paths = compute_ff_changed_paths(epoch_git, branch_git) is computed ONCE from the GLOBAL pre-absorb epoch (613d8fa) to the branch tip (ea85bf6) [merge.rs:3414]. Non-target siblings on the FastForward plan are then materialized with sync_ff_paths_in_worktree(ws_path, name, branch_oid, &ff_paths) [merge.rs:3652], which writes ONLY those paths, then set_head_detached(branch tip) + unstage_all(). A sibling whose own base epoch is BEHIND the global pre-absorb epoch never gets the paths in sibling_epoch..pre_absorb_epoch written, but its HEAD and index jump to the tip => those paths silently keep the OLD blobs and git status shows them as a local revert of the skipped commit. For continuum: sibling at 96a1fe7, ff_paths = diff(613d8fa, ea85bf6), so 613d8fa's 7 paths kept 96a1fe7 blobs. Byte-exact match to the field signature, including HEAD staying at ea85bf6 (the later sibling auto-rebase then reported 'skipped: dirty' because FF-absorb had just poisoned the worktree).\n\nContrast: sync_target_worktree_to_epoch (merge.rs:3978) does it CORRECTLY for the merge target - it diffs the workspace's OWN HEAD tree against the target tree. Only the sibling path uses the global set."}	blake3:n-EAjge-2_CFH3UELHADzvK_kxScV97C3Rlg5GEyBTI
1786555751565526	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy8BU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"REPRO (deterministic, maw 1.0.0-pre.13, no concurrency, no scale): script at /tmp/claude-1000/-home-bob-src-maw/a2a61d2d-cd82-4597-b7c0-d7f497e27bd1/scratchpad/p3m9/repro.sh\n1. maw init; commit A (f1=v1, f2=x1)\n2. maw ws create victim --from main   (victim epoch = A)\n3. maw ws create src --from main\n4. trunk-direct commit B touching f1; maw epoch sync   (epoch=B; victim STILL at A)\n5. trunk-direct commit C touching f2   (NOT epoch-synced)\n6. commit work in src; maw ws merge src --into default\nRESULT: victim HEAD=C, epoch ref=C, index=C, but f1.txt on disk = 'v1' (A content) => git status shows ' M f1.txt', an exact revert of commit B. f2.txt (in ff_paths) is correct.\nPrior repro attempts missed it because they all put the stale workspace AT the pre-absorb epoch or at the branch tip. The necessary precondition is a sibling TWO epoch-steps behind the branch tip: ws_epoch < pre_absorb_epoch < branch_tip. In continuum that gap was created by 'maw epoch sync' after a direct trunk commit, which advances epoch/current without touching live workspaces."}	blake3:6L3OkwpZlccGOqGAzYg7j1GwzqQmFiRGHvg_G33DLLU
1786556072491121	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy8RU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"MECHANISM FOUND + DETERMINISTICALLY REPRODUCED on installed pre.13. It is NOT a create-time race and NOT create at all.\n\nROOT CAUSE: `maw ws merge` FF-absorb materializes the GLOBAL epoch delta into siblings that are more than one epoch behind. In reconcile_epoch_with_branch (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs), ff_paths is computed ONCE at :3414 as compute_ff_changed_paths(global_epoch, branch), then applied to EVERY FastForward sibling at :3652 via sync_ff_paths_in_worktree(ws_path, name, branch_oid, &ff_paths) (:3901). That helper writes only those paths at branch_oid, then set_head_detached(branch) + unstage_all(). For a sibling whose own base epoch B0 is OLDER than the global pre-absorb epoch E, every path in diff(B0,E) is NEVER written, yet HEAD and index are moved to the branch tip. Those paths keep the sibling's stale B0 blobs => a fresh-looking workspace whose `git status` shows a clean revert of the skipped commit(s). The sibling classification at :3496-3535 explicitly reads the per-workspace epoch ref for base_epoch and admits base_epoch != epoch_oid into the FastForward plan, so the mismatch is reachable by construction. evaluate_ff_safety (:3449) cannot catch it either -- it also intersects against the global ff_paths only.\n\nFORENSIC PROOF against the continuum artifacts (read-only):\n- A=96a1fe7 (maw merge commit, 20:09:31Z), B=613d8fa (trunk-direct, 20:15:33Z), C=ea85bf6 (edict-hook trunk-direct, 20:23:19Z).\n- diff(A,B) = EXACTLY the 7 poisoned paths (.bones/events/2026-08.events, Justfile, notes/plan/docs/52_RELEASE_GATES_REV3.md, notes/plan/notes/PLAN_BONE_TRACEABILITY.md, notes/plan/notes/PLAN_REQUIREMENTS.json, notes/plan/tools/validate_dossier.py, notes/plan/validation-results.json). diff(B,C) = the 10 edict/AGENTS.md paths.\n- Worker stash c1258c6 (bn-3huh7 worktree) vs C: exactly those 7 paths modified. c1258c6 vs A: exactly the 10 diff(B,C) paths modified. So worktree_tree == A's tree with diff(B,C) taken from C. Its index parent 18296ca vs C: EMPTY (index == C). Same for bn-16v3x: 8d73965 vs C = the same 7 paths, index 0642a10 vs C empty.\n- That is bit-for-bit the output of sync_ff_paths_in_worktree(target=C, ff_paths=diff(B,C)) run against a worktree sitting at A: 10 paths written at C, HEAD detached to C, unstage_all -> index==C. All four observables match.\n- The absorbing merge is in the journal: integration_started bn-3j01v 20:26:31.475Z, completed 20:26:35.486Z -> 733b0fa. Unreachable cbe5b1b (bn-3j01v's own work commit, 20:26:29Z) has parent 613d8fa, proving global epoch == B at absorb time while main was already C. So the absorb range really was B..C, and the two victims were sitting at A.\n\nCORRECTION TO THE EARLIER \"VECTOR CONFIRMED: create itself materialized the stale blobs\" CALL: create is exonerated. \"Zero git/maw commands ran IN the workspace\" is true and consistent -- the corrupter was a repo-level `maw ws merge` in a DIFFERENT process reaching into sibling worktrees. It also explains why both workspaces got byte-identical poison (one absorb touched both) and why the two poison values are the epoch ref's two historical values. It implies bn-3huh7/bn-16v3x were based on A, i.e. created before B landed on trunk at 20:15:33Z, not at 20:23-20:26Z (those mtimes are C's commit and the 20:26:31 FF materialize).\n\nREPRO (deterministic, no concurrency, no scale, installed pre.13): /tmp/claude-1000/-home-bob-src-maw/a2a61d2d-cd82-4597-b7c0-d7f497e27bd1/scratchpad/wp3m9/repro_ffabsorb.sh (hit on round r003). Shape: maw init at A; `maw ws create victim --from main` (victim base=A); trunk-direct commit B touching s1/f1..f7; `maw epoch sync` (epoch->B, and CONFIRMED it does NOT touch live worktrees -- victim stays at A, this is what makes the precondition trivial to reach); trunk-direct commit C touching s2/*, no sync; create+commit in a second ws and `maw ws merge worker --into default`. Merge prints \"Absorbed 1 upstream commit(s)\" and \"victim: fast-forwarded to absorbed epoch\"; victim then has HEAD==C, ws-epoch==C, and all 7 s1 paths dirty with blobs == A. maw's own AUTO-REBASE phase then prints \"victim -- skipped: dirty\", i.e. maw notices the damage and misreads it as user edits.\n\nAUDIT VERDICTS on the assigned targets:\n1. worktree_add (crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs:20-224) -- EXONERATED as the source of this signature. index_from_tree is called twice on the SAME tree_oid derived from the requested target commit (:94-134); no epoch ref is read anywhere in maw-git. Destination is emptied by the caller before the call (crates/maw-core/src/backend/git.rs:300-303 remove_dir_all, then worktree_prune). Partial-checkout escape hatches DO exist and are worth hardening separately, but none of them can produce \"exactly the paths of one historical commit, byte-exact at its parent\": (a) outcome.collisions is never inspected (only outcome.errors at :175); gix swallows a collision as Written{bytes:0} (gix-worktree-state-0.19.0/src/checkout/chunk.rs:315-321), so a colliding path is silently left with old content; (b) outcome.delayed_paths_unknown / delayed_paths_unprocessed are likewise never inspected -- a long-running filter driver that never returns a path leaves it unwritten. Both are silent-partial-checkout risks, both would need pre-existing files in a directory the caller just deleted. Recommend checking all three fields, cheap.\n2. Epoch-delta three-way in sync/rebase.rs -- EXONERATED for this signature: it operates on trees/blobs inside the merge engine's conflict computation, never writes a worktree, and cannot run during create.\n3. replay_snapshot_with_merge_protection (workspace/working_copy.rs) -- not implicated: no merge/replay ran against these workspaces before the observed corruption, and the observed index/HEAD state is a set_head_detached+unstage_all fingerprint, not a snapshot replay.\n4. FF-absorb / sibling FF-materialize (merge.rs:3449-3660) -- GUILTY, see above. Confirms the audit-target-4 hypothesis that a repo-level merge writes into sibling worktrees, but the trigger is not a race with create: it is a plain per-sibling-epoch bug that fires every time.\n5. create command flow (workspace/create.rs) -- clean. resolve_epoch (:519-584) with --from main rev-parses the branch and never consults the epoch ref; the no --from branch auto-resyncs epoch to the branch tip before returning. Nothing between resolution and checkout reads refs/manifold/epoch/*.\nRelated sites checked and NOT defective: sync/auto_rebase.rs:465 already uses the sibling's own status.base_epoch (and is advisory only); epoch_drift.rs:218 and merge.rs:4162 use the global range but are read-only predicates/reporting.\n\nFIX: derive the materialize path set per sibling instead of from the global range, and keep the dirty-path safety check per sibling too (a sibling more than one epoch behind may have local edits in the wider range that the global predicate never checked). A worker is already implementing this in ws bn-p3m9 -- deriving the set from the sibling's own HEAD tree vs the target tree, skipping locally-dirty paths and reporting them, which is a superset of the base-epoch-ref approach and also self-heals workspaces already poisoned by the old code. Suggest that worker adopt repro_ffabsorb.sh as the regression test shape (assert `git -C .maw/workspaces/victim status --porcelain` is empty after the absorb, and that s1/f*.txt hold C's blobs).\n\nNOTE: bn-3gba's post-materialization worktree==HEAD verification would have caught this class at the FF-absorb site too, not just at create -- worth pointing it at sync_ff_paths_in_worktree's exit as well as create's."}	blake3:E1t0MBD5p13aUKCniox0uWi0adcLJzqapNmZya3y2fg
1786556092822517	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy8hU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Corroborating detail: the sibling path is the ONLY one that got this wrong. sync_target_worktree_to_epoch (merge.rs:3978-4055), which does the same job for the merge TARGET/default workspace, already resolves the workspace's own HEAD commit to a tree and materializes diff_trees(head_tree, target_tree) -- i.e. the correct per-workspace delta -- with the comment 'Equivalent to git reset --keep <oid>'. sync_ff_paths_in_worktree (merge.rs:3901) was handed a precomputed global path set instead. So the intended contract is already documented and implemented one function away; the sibling variant just never derived its own delta. That also means the fix has an in-tree reference implementation to mirror."}	blake3:fnVAiiMZHq-6Z-Uvx-koX-BRm4dIhXzm-ZHJrv88KyY
1786556123230713	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy8xU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"FIX IMPLEMENTED in workspace bn-p3m9 (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs).\n- sync_ff_paths_in_worktree now derives its materialization set from the sibling's OWN HEAD tree -> target tree diff (new helper ff_own_stale_paths), unioned with the global ff_paths floor. The global set is kept as a fallback if HEAD/diff is unreadable, so a read failure can only under-report, never regress.\n- The pre-FF safety predicate only proved dirty ∩ ff_paths = ∅, so paths OUTSIDE the absorbed range may carry genuine local edits. Those are skipped (never clobbered) and reported.\n- New FfWorktreeSync return value; reconcile_epoch_with_branch now prints '<ws>: refreshed N path(s) from earlier epoch(s) (workspace was more than one epoch behind)' and a WARNING naming any stale-but-locally-edited path that was not refreshed, with the 'maw ws sync <ws>' fix command.\nNew test file crates/maw-cli/tests/ff_absorb_stale_sibling_cli.rs (2 subprocess tests): both FAIL on unfixed merge.rs, both PASS with the fix. Verified the original signature disappears: victim worktree clean, f1 at B's content, HEAD/index/epoch ref all at the merge tip."}	blake3:74fh8AY-5l0maTXK-Mh-FWtnX42EvzpRznuwkpAIi58
1786556133726897	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy9BU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Negative control (fix scope): with the SAME precondition (victim base=A, global epoch=B, main=C), running 'maw ws sync victim' instead of a merge is CORRECT -- victim ends at HEAD=B with an empty 'git status --porcelain' and s1/* blobs equal to B. So the truncated-delta defect is isolated to the FF-absorb sibling materialize path (merge.rs:3652 -> sync_ff_paths_in_worktree); maw ws sync and sync_target_worktree_to_epoch both handle the more-than-one-epoch-behind case correctly. Repro variant: scratchpad/wp3m9/repro_sync.sh, round r004."}	blake3:FwDqFFqyv65g_i8brn0gnsUQKQVi1Q12KGHwy4VcKjk
1786556203004768	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy9RU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Negative-result stream (parallel create-race hunt): NO HIT in ~369 create-and-check cycles across 9 rounds / 8 environment shapes, stood down once the FF-absorb mechanism was proven. This is the evidence that closes out the create-time hypothesis rather than just leaving it unproven.\n\nShapes run at full scale (320 files / 20 dirs / 1.2KB-200KB, plus 7 \"hot\" B-paths at 1-5MB, 111 commits, 40 create+destroy churn cycles mixing `maw ws destroy --force` with out-of-band rmtree to strand worktree admin dirs, epoch pinned to B with main at C and asserted before every burst): large-modify, small-modify, large-mixed (B does deletes+renames), large-exec (creates issued via `maw exec <ws> -- maw ws create`), large-iopressure (background 8MB writes + find sweeps), small-mixed-heavychurn (60-workspace churn), epochflip-large/small (epoch ref flipped A<->B every 10ms under the creates), dirty-root-large/dirty-root-flip (root default workspace left holding A blobs on B paths, unstaged), plus persistent workspaces and concurrent `maw ws advance`. Bursts: 2/4/8-way concurrent `maw ws create --from main` racing `git worktree prune`, `maw ws merge`, `maw ws destroy` mid-flight and `maw epoch sync`, at 0/50/200ms staggers.\n\nSECONDARY FINDINGS worth their own bones:\n(a) Concurrent create can die on a git index lock with no retry. Under 8-way concurrent `maw ws create --from main`: \"Error: Failed to create workspace: `worktree add` failed: git backend error: failed to write worktree index: Could not acquire lock for index file\", exit 1, no workspace left behind, no backoff. maw serializes creates through .maw/manifold/locks/create for its own metadata, but the `worktree_add` index write (crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs:120-126) still races. Retry-with-backoff there would make concurrent agent spin-up robust.\n(b) Stranded worktree admin dirs are auto-pruned by ordinary maw commands, so a prune backlog never accumulates naturally in the field -- the \"~40 destroyed worktrees\" detail from the field report is not a standing condition and was a red herring.\n(c) Independent corroboration of the root cause: with epoch=B and main=C, `maw ws merge` is REFUSED by the divergence guard whenever an in-flight workspace touches the FF range. So the FF-absorb materialize path is only reachable once the global epoch has been advanced past a sibling's own base AND no in-flight workspace touches the absorbed range -- exactly the \"sibling base older than global epoch\" precondition, and exactly why a create-time hunt could never hit it.\n\nTESTING GUIDANCE for the fix: `git status --porcelain` alone is NOT a sufficient detector for this bug class -- the index stat cache can mask it. The regression test / DST oracle should compare trees: throwaway GIT_INDEX_FILE, `read-tree HEAD` + `add -A` + `write-tree`, assert equal to `HEAD^{tree}`. Harness + validated positive control at scratchpad/wp3m9/{harness.py,selftest.py}."}	blake3:l3cS53Nx0jwDXZAUoOtBN5twECIFP0wg5syYV8hS7j0
1786556307345630	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy9hU		item.comment	bn-1du0	{"body":"FIX LANDED in workspace bn-1du0 (commit 5d811517, unmerged — lead reviews). Root cause confirmed as diagnosed: apply_merge_drivers fired Regenerate on partition.unique AND on cleanly-diff3-resolved shared paths.\n\nWHAT CHANGED (src/merge/build_phase.rs): new DriverScope gate {Unique, SharedResolved, SharedConflict}. Unique -> NO driver runs at all (sole side taken verbatim). SharedResolved -> ours/theirs still apply, regenerate does not. SharedConflict -> all kinds fire as the resolution. D/F-clash paths excluded (a driver would publish the file side and drop the directory side).\n\nSCOPE NOTE FOR LEAD: the unique-path gate also covers ours/theirs, not just regenerate — 'ours' on a unique path reverted the only workspace that touched the file, the same silent-revert class. This matches git, which invokes a merge driver only when BOTH sides changed the file. Two integration tests pin both halves (ours_driver_never_reverts_a_unique_path, ours_driver_still_overrides_a_shared_path). Revert to regenerate-only if you want the narrower fix.\n\nSECOND BUG FOUND + FIXED: a failed non-required regenerate driver removed the conflict record and then fell back to 'normal merge' with nothing resolved — the merge published BASE content and lost both sides silently. This is a plausible mechanism for field-report Case 2 (12-line hunk vanished, no Cargo.lock hunk in merge 3690dbb) whenever cargo generate-lockfile failed. Conflict records are now taken, held, and restored when the command fails.\n\nVISIBILITY (was silent): NOTE line per rewritten path on stderr (\"NOTE: merge driver 'cargo generate-lockfile' regenerated Cargo.lock (textual conflict)\"); driver_rewrites[] in ws merge --format json; new MergeDriversApplied merge event (maw merge events); BuildPhaseOutput.driver_rewrites. 'maw ws merge --plan' heading is now 'Merge drivers that will fire:' and lists only drivers that really will.\n\nTESTS: 4 new unit tests (build_phase_regenerate_driver_skips_unique_path, _skips_clean_shared_merge, _reports_rewrite_on_conflict, build_phase_regenerate_failure_restores_conflict_when_not_required) + 7 new integration tests in tests/merge_driver_regenerate_bn_1du0.rs (regenerate_driver_never_fires_on_unique_path, _never_fires_on_clean_shared_merge, _fires_on_true_conflict_and_reports_note, _rewrite_appears_in_merge_json, ours_driver_never_reverts_a_unique_path, ours_driver_still_overrides_a_shared_path, failed_optional_regenerate_restores_the_conflict). All use a sentinel driver command (printf REGENERATED > Cargo.lock) so no cargo and no network.\n\nEXISTING TEST CHANGED DELIBERATELY: build_phase_regenerate_failure_reported_as_validation_failure used ONE workspace (unique path) to make the driver run; that no longer fires by design, so it now uses two workspaces editing the same line. Assertions unchanged.\n\njust check: PASS (fmt, clippy -D warnings, full test suite, DST g1-g4 + determinism, contract_drift). 84 'test result: ok', zero 'test result: FAILED'.\n\nNOT DONE (deliberate, out of scope): no conservative-regen command and no config switch to disable the built-in defaults — the gate alone removes the data loss. DST oracle for driver rewrites not added."}	blake3:k5UeXLymWymfYPUiAiswFC4y3XNfpYZ0x_J-4hjm5c0
1786556393260188	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy9xU		item.comment	bn-39zu	{"body":"Implemented and committed in workspace bn-39zu (commit 134dc53d), ready to merge.\n\n1. Rewind warning (default on, warn-only): src/merge/build_phase.rs adds\n   detect_rewind_warnings(), called in both run_pipeline (real merges) and\n   run_build_phase_with_inputs (test/plan path), against the real source\n   PatchSets before epoch-delta injection so attribution always names a\n   genuine workspace. For each Added/Modified change whose blob OID differs\n   from the epoch tip's blob at that path, walks epoch's first-parent\n   history (bounded 100 commits, commit-major so the walk stops the moment\n   every candidate path has matched) comparing blob OIDs only via new\n   GitRepo::blob_oid_at_commit (crates/maw-git: repo.rs trait + objects_impl.rs\n   impl + gix_repo.rs delegate) -- no blob content is ever read, so cost is\n   independent of file size. New BuildPhaseOutput.rewind_warnings field.\n   CLI (crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs) prints a loud \"  WARNING: ...\"\n   line in text mode and folds the same messages into MergeSuccessOutput's\n   existing warnings[] JSON field. Never blocks the merge.\n\n2. Append-only config (opt-in, refuses): MergeConfig.append_only: Vec<String>\n   glob list added to crates/maw-core/src/config.rs. New\n   assert_append_only_preserved() in merge.rs runs after BUILD (post any\n   --resolve conflict patching, before VALIDATE) against the final candidate\n   tree: for each resolved path matching a glob, if the epoch tip had content\n   there, the merged result must keep those bytes as an exact prefix (a\n   deletion or non-prefix rewrite is a violation); a brand-new file never\n   violates. Refuses with bail! naming every violating path + the --force\n   hint; --force bypasses and folds a warning per path into warnings[]/stderr.\n\nTests: config.rs unit tests append_only_defaults_empty + parse_append_only_globs.\ntests/merge_rewind_guard_bn_39zu.rs -- 8 end-to-end CLI tests: rewind warning\nin JSON + text output, non-rewind control (new content), immediate-previous-\nchange revert (still flagged), deletion-is-not-a-rewind control,\nappend-only refusal on middle-line deletion + --force override succeeding,\npure-append success (silent), whole-file deletion refusal, brand-new-file\nexemption. All 33 tests in that file pass; full `just check` (fmt-check,\nclippy, unit+integration+doctests across the workspace, dst-fast,\ncontract-drift) passed clean, exit 0.\n\nScope cuts: rewind-warning surfacing wired only into the real `maw ws merge`\nsuccess path (not --check/--plan/--conflicts preview paths) -- those callers\nstill get BuildPhaseOutput.rewind_warnings on the struct if a future patch\nwants to surface it there too, just not printed/JSON'd yet. Ancestor walk\nbound is 100 commits (bone suggested \"e.g. 200\"); chosen to keep an\nordinary merge cheap while still covering realistic staleness windows --\neasy to bump (REWIND_MAX_ANCESTOR_WALK constant in build_phase.rs) if real\nusage shows it's too shallow."}	blake3:dHjgNCoxXkpYw9jj9ycFnUilHV9ZF_0XFvFAlJvT4HQ
1786556412183348	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy-BU		item.comment	bn-1du0	{"body":"Lead review PASSED (commit 5d811517 in ws bn-1du0). Verified independently: 7/7 integration tests + 32 unit tests green. Fix: DriverScope gate — no driver on unique paths, regenerate only on real textual conflict, ours/theirs still override shared paths; D/F clashes excluded; failed non-required regenerate restores the displaced conflict record (plausible field Case 2 mechanism); NOTE per rewrite + driver_rewrites in JSON + MergeDriversApplied event. Merge deferred until sibling workers finish."}	blake3:Yl-k154vQ6XXK0MkT_Z6z9Duvui-JhOOxl78xSmr-Mo
1786556507760204	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy-RU		item.create	bn-2mio	{"description":"Found during bn-p3m9 investigation (2026-08-12), harness with 8-way concurrent `maw ws create`:\ncreate dies with `failed to write worktree index: Could not acquire lock for index file`, exit 1,\nno backoff or retry. Site: crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs:120-126 (worktree index write).\n\nmaw's create lock covers manifold metadata but not the git index write, so concurrent creates\n(or a create racing any other index writer) hit the raw gix lock error.\n\nFix options: bounded retry with backoff on the index-lock acquisition, or widen the create lock\nto cover the index write. Error message should name the workspace and suggest retrying.\n\nRepro: scratchpad wp3m9 harness (bn-p3m9 session, 2026-08-12), 8 parallel creates, 0ms stagger.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["reliability"],"title":"Concurrent ws create fails on git index lock with no retry"}	blake3:8BKcNwtMaYkivjuCraGrJb-iXiF-cKq6N_elWre6MRk
1786556507909938	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy-hU		item.create	bn-2r7a	{"description":"Found during bn-p3m9 audit (2026-08-12) of crates/maw-git/src/worktree_impl.rs `worktree_add`:\nthe gix checkout `outcome.collisions` and `delayed_paths_unknown` / `delayed_paths_unprocessed`\nfields are never inspected. gix swallows collisions as `Written{bytes:0}`, so a collision or an\nunprocessed delayed path yields a silently incomplete worktree while create reports success.\n\nNot the bn-p3m9 mechanism (that was FF-absorb sibling materialization), but the same failure\nclass: worktree does not match HEAD after an operation that claims it does.\n\nFix: after checkout, if collisions or delayed-path fields are non-empty, fail create loudly\nnaming the paths (or repair by re-checking out those paths). Add a unit test forcing a collision.\nThe bn-3gba post-materialization verify provides defense-in-depth, but worktree_add should not\nrely on it.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["reliability"],"title":"worktree_add ignores gix checkout collisions/delayed-paths outcome (silent partial checkout risk)"}	blake3:KKdDrf2qYa8DXKYEWqUhcPKXZe2jbIODsazVsq0Symk
1786556554280216	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy-xU		item.comment	bn-1du0	{"body":"Fix implemented in workspace bn-1du0 (commits 5d811517 + 95894e53, branch tip 95894e53). NOT merged — lead reviews.\n\nWHAT CHANGED\n- src/merge/build_phase.rs: new private enum DriverScope { Unique, SharedResolved, SharedConflict } computed per path in apply_merge_drivers. Gate:\n  * Unique (one workspace touched the path) -> NO driver of any kind fires; sole side's content taken verbatim. This also closes the 'ours reverts the only side' variant (item 3): 'ours' on a unique path used to replace the sole workspace's change with the epoch blob.\n  * SharedResolved (2+ sides, diff3/AST merged cleanly) -> 'ours'/'theirs' still apply (explicit user 'pick a side' declarations), 'regenerate' does NOT.\n  * SharedConflict (2+ sides, textual resolution failed) -> every driver kind may fire, as the conflict resolution.\n  * D/F clash paths (partition.df_clash_paths() / ConflictReason::FileDirectory) are skipped entirely — resolving one with a driver would publish the file side and drop the directory side.\n- Conflict status threading: no new plumbing was needed. ResolveResult.conflicts IS the per-path resolution status coming out of resolve.rs; apply_merge_drivers already receives the whole ResolveResult, so the gate is a BTreeSet<PathBuf> built from those records (minus FileDirectory reasons) before the conflict vec is mutated.\n- Regenerate failure safety: with the gate, a regenerate driver only ever displaces a real conflict, so 'required = false' + failing command must give the conflict back. Added take_conflict_path() + DriverPass.regenerate_conflicts; conflicts are now removed only after run_regenerate_drivers actually returns content for the path, and unregenerated paths get their ConflictRecord restored. Previously the record was dropped up-front, which would have published epoch content and lost both sides.\n- Reporting (item 2, previously silent): new pub struct DriverRewrite { path, kind, command, reason } + DriverRewriteReason { TextualConflict, DriverOverride } in build_phase; BuildPhaseOutput gains driver_rewrites: Vec<DriverRewrite>. Every rewrite prints 'NOTE: merge driver <cmd-or-kind> regenerated|rewrote <path> (<reason>)' on stderr from the BUILD phase (stderr keeps --format json parseable). Also surfaced as: MergeSuccessOutput.driver_rewrites in 'ws merge --format json' (new DriverRewriteJson), and a new merge event MergeEventKind::MergeDriversApplied { sources, into, paths, kinds, reasons } appended in workspace/merge.rs (emit_merge_drivers_applied) and rendered by 'maw merge events' (merge_cmd.rs print_event_line). Only rewrites that actually changed the outcome are recorded.\n- Plan truthfulness (item 4): build_driver_infos() now takes (overlaps, conflict_paths, config) instead of all touched paths — unique paths are never listed, and 'regenerate' is listed only for paths that actually conflict. Heading changed to 'Merge drivers that will fire:'.\n\nTESTS ADDED\ntests/merge_driver_regenerate_bn_1du0.rs (new, end-to-end through the maw binary, sentinel driver 'printf REGENERATED > Cargo.lock' so no cargo/network):\n- regenerate_driver_never_fires_on_unique_path (a: byte-identical survival)\n- regenerate_driver_never_fires_on_clean_shared_merge (b)\n- regenerate_driver_fires_on_true_conflict_and_reports_note (c: driver output wins + NOTE printed)\n- regenerate_driver_rewrite_appears_in_merge_json\n- ours_driver_never_reverts_a_unique_path (item 3)\n- ours_driver_still_overrides_a_shared_path\n- failed_optional_regenerate_restores_the_conflict\nsrc/merge/build_phase.rs unit tests:\n- build_phase_regenerate_driver_skips_unique_path\n- build_phase_regenerate_driver_skips_clean_shared_merge\n- build_phase_regenerate_driver_reports_rewrite_on_conflict\n- build_phase_regenerate_failure_restores_conflict_when_not_required\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs unit tests:\n- plan_omits_regenerate_driver_for_cleanly_merged_path\n- plan_lists_regenerate_driver_for_conflicting_path\n- plan_lists_ours_driver_for_any_overlap\n(d) config.rs default-driver test (Cargo.lock + package-lock.json Regenerate defaults) untouched and green; the pre-existing driver tests (build_phase_ours_driver_keeps_epoch_version, build_phase_theirs_driver_requires_single_workspace, both regenerate resolution tests) all still pass unchanged because they use shared conflicting paths.\n\nGATE: 'just check' run synchronously on the committed tree — EXIT=0, 84 suites, 3224 tests passed, 0 'test result: FAILED', 0 errors, 0 clippy warnings.\n\nLEFT OUT / RISKS\n- 'theirs' still errors on a multi-workspace path ('requires exactly one workspace'). Since drivers now fire only on shared paths, a 'theirs' driver on a genuinely 2-sided path errors rather than picking a side. N-way 'theirs' has never had defined semantics; defining it (e.g. last source in sorted order) is a separate call.\n- 'ours'/'theirs' deliberately still override cleanly merged SHARED paths — only 'regenerate' is conflict-gated there. Rationale: those are explicit user declarations of 'do not merge this file'; 'regenerate' is a built-in default nobody opted into.\n- No CHANGELOG entry (avoids conflicting with other in-flight workspaces; release tooling owns it).\n- Behavior change worth calling out in release notes: a repo relying on a configured 'ours' driver to pin a path even when a single workspace edits it will now see that workspace's edit land."}	blake3:WBbjwQe32F1noT-hT8rEnaENCvdfSG3P-gE1VdC-V3U
1786556651675586	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy_BU		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Fix committed in workspace bn-p3m9 as 7405e147. 'just check' run SYNCHRONOUSLY in the workspace: EXIT=0, zero 'test result: FAILED', new ff_absorb_stale_sibling_cli tests ran and passed inside it. NOT merged, NOT pushed, NOT installed - lead review pending.\n\nFOLLOW-UPS for the lead:\n1. bn-3gba (post-materialization worktree==HEAD verify + DST oracle) is still worth landing: it is the class-level net. This fix closes the one known hole; the oracle catches the next one. A DST oracle asserting 'clean workspace worktree tree == HEAD tree after every materialization step' would have caught this bug directly.\n2. Same class, NOT fixed here: epoch_drift.rs auto_advance_if_safe documents (lines 274-282) that sibling baselines are intentionally left at the old epoch because 'subsequent merges will observe is_stale = true for those siblings and run the normal rebase path'. That assumption was exactly what was false - the FF-absorb FastForward plan is NOT the normal rebase path. Worth re-reading that comment now that the invariant is enforced.\n3. Field-report correction to send to continuum-dev: the workspaces were NOT freshly created at 20:23-20:26; they were created at 20:01 and had been sitting at 96a1fe7 since the 20:09 merge. Their 'create materialized it' conclusion (and mine on the earlier comment) was wrong. The real trigger is 'maw epoch sync' after a direct trunk commit leaving live workspaces two epoch-steps behind, then a merge that FF-absorbs. Workaround for them until the fix ships: run 'maw ws sync' (or 'maw ws advance') on live workspaces right after any 'maw epoch sync', or avoid direct trunk commits while workspaces are live."}	blake3:-skfOBIIE4N5xY3DSs0o_B4YWSnIlcllAgwyOtTCSGI
1786556667656455	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy_RU		item.comment	bn-39zu	{"body":"Pure-rewind merge guard implemented and committed in workspace bn-39zu at 134dc53d1816dcda0358df08bb26ed8065311d17 (parent 61e8c828). NOTE FOR LEAD: this workspace was concurrently edited by another agent/session while I worked in it (same .maw/workspaces/bn-39zu/ dir) — they built a complementary \"append-only config, --force refusal\" defense (item 2 of your comment) on top of my draft and committed both together before I could commit myself. I verified the final committed state end to end; see below.\n\nMy scope (pure rewind, warn-only):\n- src/merge/build_phase.rs: RewindWarning struct + detect_rewind_warnings(), wired into both run_pipeline (real merge) and run_build_phase_with_inputs (test/plan path). Walks epoch_before's first-parent history (capped 100 commits, commit-major so the walk is shared across all changed paths and stops once every candidate matches) comparing blob OIDs only (uses the new GitRepo::blob_oid_at_commit primitive the other session added to crates/maw-git — OID-only, never reads blob bytes, so cost is file-size independent). BuildPhaseOutput.rewind_warnings carries results.\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs: prints a loud \"  WARNING: <ws> rewinds <path> to its content at <short-oid> (<N> commits behind the epoch). If this is unintentional, the workspace holds a stale copy.\" line in text mode, and folds the same message into warnings[] in --format json. Warn-only, never blocks. Deletions and genuinely-new content never trigger it (verified by tests).\n- tests/merge_rewind_guard_bn_39zu.rs: I authored merge_warns_on_pure_rewind_to_older_epoch_blob, merge_text_output_prints_loud_warning_line_on_rewind, merge_does_not_warn_on_genuinely_new_content, merge_warns_but_succeeds_on_revert_of_immediately_previous_change, merge_does_not_warn_on_deletion. The other session appended 4 more (append-only item 2) tests. All 8 pass.\n\nVerification of the final committed tree: `just check` exits 0 clean (fmt-check, clippy -D warnings, cargo test + cargo test -p maw-cli, dst-fast, contract-drift all green, 0 FAILED anywhere). Ran cargo test --workspace separately too (broader than just check) and found ONE pre-existing unrelated failure, checkout_impl::tests::checkout_detach_removes_stale_tracked_files in maw-git (git-worktree --force semantics vs installed git 2.55.0) — reproduces identically on trunk root with zero bn-39zu changes applied, not part of the just check gate, not touched by this bone.\n\nDesign notes: commits_behind starts at 1 (immediate parent). A legitimate revert of only the last change still warns (indistinguishable from an accident at this layer) but never blocks. Cap of 100 first-parent commits per bone spec.\n\nRecommend the lead double check who else was in this workspace concurrently (git identity on the commit is the generic repo default, not diagnostic) — flagging in case a duplicate worker was dispatched on this bone."}	blake3:0naNNvmUWOmhzbNzjHVlZ1pI-zT28FjytDZn3zLBCG0
1786556726368697	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy_hU		item.comment	bn-39zu	{"body":"Lead review of 134dc53d (maw-dev, this session): APPROVED pending merge-time test run. Verified: rewind walk is OID-only/bounded/commit-major with early dropout, degrades to no-warning on git errors; append-only guard runs on resolved_paths which includes unique-path passthroughs and deletions (no unique-path hole — confirmed in resolve.rs resolve_partition_with_attrs); merge_base_epoch = frozen.epoch (correct base); JSON warnings[] + text WARNING both wired; blob_oid_at_commit touches only tree objects. Nits: (1) detect_rewind_warnings doc claims new files are skipped but code checks them against ancestor history — behavior is right (catches resurrected stale files), fix the doc; (2) rewind warnings not in --check/plan preview paths (declared scope cut, field available on BuildPhaseOutput). Worker ran just check clean (exit 0). Trunk stash@{0} holds the worker's accidental trunk edits — drop after merge."}	blake3:hLPnMyQAxgjY23kgZ8V9rL_s_B_jcqxZFZzFOr3C5Jk
1786556816816263	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEy_xU		item.comment	bn-1du0	{"body":"Lead review of 5d811517+95894e53 as one unit (maw-dev, this session): APPROVED pending merge-time test run. Verified in source: DriverScope gate (Unique: no driver ever fires, closes ours-on-unique data loss too; SharedResolved: ours/theirs apply, regenerate does not; SharedConflict: all fire), D/F clash paths excluded from driver resolution, conflicted_paths computed from ResolveResult before mutation, run_pending_regenerations restores displaced ConflictRecords when a non-required regenerate command fails (old code silently published base content — plausible mechanism for field Case 2), NOTE lines on stderr keep JSON parseable, driver_rewrites in JSON + MergeDriversApplied event, plan display now lists regenerate only for conflicting paths. Release-notes flag: repos relying on a configured ours driver to pin a path against single-workspace edits will now see the edit land. Residual: theirs on a genuinely 2-sided shared path errors (previously unreachable); defining N-way theirs semantics is out of scope. Worker just check exit 0, 3224 tests."}	blake3:3IHEvirMbJ_H6qDFwVSr56SCYsmSXKFHFAL_U12h72I
1786557516875011	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEygBY		item.comment	bn-3gba	{"body":"DONE (workspace bn-3gba, commit b9fa1111 — NOT merged, lead reviews).\n\nWHAT LANDED\n- crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/materialize_verify.rs (new): detect -> preserve -> repair -> re-verify -> record.\n- KEY DESIGN CHANGE vs the bone's pitfall note: detection compares TREES, not status. git status / git diff HEAD / gix status_head_to_worktree all short-circuit on the index STAT CACHE, and the corrupter rewrites HEAD+index AFTER writing stale bytes (set_head_detached + index realign) — so the index can hold the CORRECT blob OID stamped with the STALE file's stat data and every stat-based check reports clean. Detection = throwaway index seeded by read-tree HEAD (zeroed stat data) -> git add -A (forces re-hash) -> write-tree -> diff-tree vs HEAD tree. status_head_to_worktree remains only as a degraded fallback if git plumbing fails (bn-pfh7 variant honoured). Regression pinned by crates/maw-cli/tests/materialize_verify_stat_cache_bn_3gba.rs, which reproduces the mask and asserts the verifier still catches it.\n- PRIME INVARIANT: pre-repair bytes are pinned to refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/materialize-<ts> BEFORE any overwrite (capture.rs: new capture_before_materialize_repair sharing capture_before_clean's alternate-index body). Capture failure DISABLES the repair — divergence left in place + reported beats content destroyed unpreserved.\n- Reporting: loud stderr-only WARNING (stdout stays JSON-clean) naming paths + the pin; JSON artifact .maw/manifold/artifacts/ws/<ws>/materialize-repair/<ts>.json (one file per event, destroy-record convention); OpPayload::Annotate key 'materialize-repair' in the oplog (additive, no schema break) visible in maw ws history.\n- Scope: only M/D/T. A/Untracked name paths absent from HEAD, so 'repair' = DELETE = Prime-Invariant violation. Never touched.\n- ff_materialize_blob in merge.rs now delegates to the shared mode-preserving writer (no duplicate symlink/exec-bit logic).\n\nHOOK SITES (exact)\n1. create.rs create_with_output, after backend.create + template artifact -> MaterializeOp::Create.\n2. sync/checks.rs sync_worktree_to_epoch_inner, after checkout_detach -> SyncFastForward. Single choke point: covers ws sync (text+json), sync --all, auto_sync_if_stale, sync_worktree_to_epoch_quiet.\n3. merge.rs reconcile_epoch_with_branch: after rebase_sibling_for_absorb Ok when conflicts==0 && worktree_updated -> FfAbsorbReplay; after sync_ff_paths_in_worktree when !dirty -> FfAbsorbFastForward.\n4. sync/auto_rebase.rs new verify_sibling_materialization(), called from rebase_one_sibling, fires ONLY on SiblingResult::RebasedClean -> AutoRebase.\n\nNOT HOOKED (skip-scoping, deliberate)\n- snapshot / preserve-and-replay (working_copy::snapshot_working_copy, dirty-trunk preserve/replay): dirty state is the INPUT.\n- ws sync when it replays local commits (rebase_workspace path): may legitimately end conflicted with marker bytes on disk.\n- RebasedWithConflicts / RebasedWithConflictsRefsOnly: conflict-as-data is first-class.\n- RebasedCleanRefsOnly: worktree update intentionally skipped, worktree is EXPECTED to lag HEAD.\n- FF-absorb SiblingPlan::FastForward { dirty: true }: the safety predicate PROVED the dirty paths are disjoint from the FF range; repairing there would eat live agent work.\n- UpToDate/SkippedInUse/SkippedDirty/SkippedInProgress/Failed: nothing materialized.\n- ws advance: not a hooked site, so the DST oracle disarms after it too (a gate with no fix behind it is not actionable).\nPinned by tests/materialize_verify_bn_3gba.rs: dirty_sibling_edits_survive_merge_auto_rebase_untouched, dirty_sibling_edits_survive_ff_absorb_untouched, clean_create_and_ff_sync_are_silent (all in just check).\n\nFAULT INJECTION\n- New FailpointAction::Corrupt(PathBuf) + CORRUPT_BYTES in maw-core/src/failpoints.rs; env-expressible as MAW_FP=NAME=corrupt:<abs-path>. Unlike the crash-shaped actions it perturbs and CONTINUES — that is what makes it a partial-materialization primitive. New site FP_CREATE_AFTER_MATERIALIZE (added to KNOWN_FAILPOINTS) fires after the checkout, before the verify.\n- crates/maw-cli/tests/materialize_verify_bn_3gba.rs (needs --features failpoints, uses CARGO_BIN_EXE_maw so no nested cargo build): corrupted_create_is_detected_repaired_and_reported asserts create still exits 0, the WARNING names the path + bn-p3m9, the pin holds the PRE-repair bytes, the file is byte-identical to HEAD, git status is clean, the artifact JSON is well-formed, and maw ws history carries the annotation. Plus clean_create_produces_no_warning_and_no_artifact and untracked_scratch_is_never_treated_as_divergence.\n\nDST ORACLE\n- crates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_worktree.rs: CleanMaterialization (bn-2bcx pattern — new oracle module, git-CLI-only independent verifier, read-only). Expected-dirty model: WsCreate/Commit/Sync/Advance(ok) -> clean; EditFiles/Recover/Sync|Advance(fail) -> dirty; Merge(ok) keeps siblings armed (THE assertion); Merge(fail) disarms all live workspaces because the faulted tier aborts merges mid-flight and a half-written sibling worktree is a fault artifact, not a defect; default/trunk never judged (bn-1xmk territory). Exhaustive match on Op (no _ arm) so a new op forces a decision.\n- Wired into tests/dst_production_tier.rs after every op (both the seed loop and drive_regression_plan), with a checks_run non-vacuity liveness assert.\n\nTEST EVIDENCE (all synchronous, full output grepped for 'test result: FAILED' = 0)\n- just check: EXIT=0, 86 'test result: ok' blocks, 0 FAILED. (dst-fast smoke tier included, green.)\n- just sg1-materialize-check (new gate): 3 passed.\n- just sg1-per-commit: 64/64 seeds clean, 0 violations; sg1_generator_is_byte_identical_per_seed PASSES => default DST profile seed->plan stream unperturbed. maw-scenario untouched (git status clean for that crate); cargo test -p maw-scenario 18 passed.\n- just sg1-production-tier (default 16x24): 384 op-steps, 336 clean-materialization checks, 0 violations.\n- Faulted tier (DST_TRACES=6 DST_STEPS=24, --ignored dst_production_tier_survives_faults): 144 op-steps, 4 faults injected, 152 clean-materialization checks, 0 violations.\n- just sg1-faithful-clippy / sg1-assurance-clippy / sg2-bench-clippy: all EXIT=0.\n- tests/ci_lane_wiring.rs + contract_drift: green.\n\nCI WIRING (bn-1n2b)\n- New gate recipe sg1-materialize-check in the Justfile, referenced by .github/workflows/dst-faithful.yml (the job that already builds the failpoints binary). ci_lane_wiring.rs enforces it stays wired. The pure/library-level parts (skip-scoping, artifact schema, stat-cache regression, Corrupt semantics, oracle state machine) are plain tests and run in just check.\n\nFOR THE LEAD — one tradeoff to weigh\nThe tree comparison costs one content hash of the worktree per hooked op (~100ms on maw's own 1.4k-file/36MB checkout; gitignored trees are pruned, not walked). There is no cheap-and-correct hybrid: short-circuiting on a clean 'git status' would reintroduce exactly the stat-cache mask this class hides behind. If the cost is unacceptable on very large repos, the right lever is a config opt-out (or sampling), not a status-based fast path."}	blake3:eGQRieNOXrPXz19phZC56hFxLgTeLzX3EFTS1w2MVxU
1786557569938881	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEygRY		item.comment	bn-3gba	{"body":"Implemented in workspace bn-3gba, commit b9fa1111 (16 files, +2952/-59). NOT merged/pushed; bone left OPEN.\n\nNEW MODULE crates/maw-cli/src/workspace/materialize_verify.rs\n- Detection compares TREES, not `git status`: throwaway GIT_INDEX_FILE + `read-tree HEAD` (zeroed stat) + `add -A` (forces re-hash) + `write-tree` + `diff-tree -z --no-renames` vs HEAD^{tree}. Reason: every stat-cache-based check (git status, git diff HEAD, gix status_head_to_worktree) can be MASKED by this class, because the corrupter rewrites HEAD+index after writing stale bytes. status_head_to_worktree remains only as a degraded fallback if git plumbing fails. Measured cost ~100ms on maw's own 1430-file/36MB checkout.\n- Scope: M/D/T only. A/untracked never counted (repair would mean DELETING); renames decompose to caught D + ignored A.\n- PRESERVE-BEFORE-REPAIR: pins pre-repair bytes at refs/manifold/recovery/<ws>/materialize-<ts> via the capture_before_clean alternate-index technique (refactored into capture_paths_to_ref). Capture failure DISABLES the repair (fail-safe).\n- Repair: re-materializes each path from HEAD mode-preserving (merge.rs's ff_materialize_blob now delegates to the shared writer), unstage_all, then re-verifies with the SAME tree comparison.\n- Records: loud stderr WARNING (paths + pin + evidence path + bn-p3m9 tag), JSON artifact .maw/manifold/artifacts/ws/<ws>/materialize-repair/<ts>.json, and an oplog Annotate op (key \"materialize-repair\"). Never fails the caller's op.\n\nCALL SITES INSTRUMENTED (4)\n- create.rs create_with_output, after backend.create (MaterializeOp::Create)\n- sync/checks.rs sync_worktree_to_epoch_inner, after checkout_detach (SyncFastForward) — entry already refuses dirty, so clean-at-epoch is the contract\n- merge.rs reconcile_epoch_with_branch: SiblingPlan::Replay when conflicts==0 && worktree_updated (FfAbsorbReplay), and SiblingPlan::FastForward only when !dirty (FfAbsorbFastForward) — this is the site the lead root-caused as the actual bn-p3m9 mechanism (sync_ff_paths_in_worktree applies the GLOBAL epoch delta to every sibling then moves HEAD+index, so siblings on an older base keep stale blobs on un-covered paths; the repair completes the materialization from HEAD)\n- sync/auto_rebase.rs rebase_one_sibling on SiblingResult::RebasedClean only\n\nDELIBERATELY SKIPPED: FF-absorb FastForward{dirty:true} (predicate proved edits disjoint, preserved on purpose), RebasedCleanRefsOnly / RebasedWithConflicts* (worktree intentionally lags / conflict-as-data), SkippedDirty/UpToDate/Failed, sync rebase path, snapshot/preserve-and-replay, merge target + dirty-trunk. Known coverage gap: a dirty FF-absorb sibling can still be corrupted undetected — indistinguishable from the agent's own edits without a per-sibling delta.\n\nDST ORACLE: crates/maw-assurance/src/oracle_worktree.rs::CleanMaterialization (feature `oracles`), wired into tests/dst_production_tier.rs run_seed + drive_regression_plan, plus a `clean_materialization_checks` liveness counter. Tracks an expected-dirty set from the op stream (+ success verdict) and asserts every live, non-default, expected-clean workspace has worktree==HEAD, using the same tree comparison. Read-only: no ops generated, no weights changed, seed->plan byte stream unchanged. Evidence: 2545 checks / 0 violations at DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48; 336 checks / 0 violations at the default budget.\n\nFAILPOINT: FailpointAction::Corrupt(path) + `corrupt:<abs-path>` MAW_FP action + FP_CREATE_AFTER_MATERIALIZE (registered in KNOWN_FAILPOINTS, fires after checkout / before verify).\n\nTESTS\n- crates/maw-cli/tests/materialize_verify_bn_3gba.rs (needs --features failpoints): corrupted_create_is_detected_repaired_and_reported, clean_create_produces_no_warning_and_no_artifact, untracked_scratch_is_never_treated_as_divergence\n- crates/maw-cli/tests/materialize_verify_stat_cache_bn_3gba.rs (DEFAULT lane): materialize_verify_survives_index_stat_cache_refresh (forces a real stat-cache mask — asserts `git status --porcelain` is EMPTY — then proves the tree detector still catches/preserves/repairs), clean_workspace_with_rewritten_index_is_not_divergence, untracked_scratch_is_not_divergence_under_tree_comparison\n- tests/materialize_verify_bn_3gba.rs (DEFAULT lane): clean_create_and_ff_sync_are_silent, dirty_sibling_edits_survive_merge_auto_rebase_untouched, dirty_sibling_edits_survive_ff_absorb_untouched\n- 11 oracle unit tests + module unit tests for divergence scoping / artifact schema / Corrupt action.\n\nCI: new gate `just sg1-materialize-check` wired into .github/workflows/dst-faithful.yml (bn-1n2b convention; ci_lane_wiring green). Everything else rides the default `cargo test` lane.\n\nGATE: `just check` EXIT=0, zero `test result: FAILED`. `just sg1-assurance-clippy` and `just sg1-materialize-check` green.\n\nSEPARATE FINDING (not caused by this change): at DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48 the production tier reports 4 pre-existing SiblingRefFaithfulness (bn-rah2, FF-absorb sibling-reset) violations on seeds 0/15/18 — committed sibling blobs unreachable after a merge. Default gate budget (16x24) is clean, so no gate turns red. This code only writes worktree files, calls unstage_all and ADDS refs, so it cannot orphan a commit. Same FF-absorb sibling family as the bn-p3m9 mechanism — worth triaging together.\n\nANOMALY: session collision. Files in this workspace were edited and the work was committed (b9fa1111) by another agent/tooling mid-task. Content verified intact and complete; nothing reverted."}	blake3:76xew_OEvcsH5nveJV125n562aE4eiVp4iy2TsjY7H0
1786557703472168	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyghY		item.comment	bn-3gba	{"body":"Lead review of b9fa1111 (maw-dev, this session): APPROVED pending merge-time test run. Verified in source: tree-based detection (throwaway index read-tree/add -A/write-tree vs HEAD^{tree}) with status_head_to_worktree only as degraded fallback on plumbing failure; capture failure DISABLES repair (fail-safe, divergence left+reported); index realigned then tree-based re-verify (the spot most likely to be stat-masked); artifact+oplog+WARNING; never fails the parent op. Call sites: create, sync FF (dirty-refused on entry), FfAbsorbReplay (conflicts==0 && worktree_updated), FfAbsorbFastForward only when !dirty — dirty siblings correctly skipped (repair could destroy real edits; fundamental gap until bn-p3m9 fix lands). ff_materialize_blob refactored to one shared mode-preserving writer for absorb+repair. DST oracle read-only, 2545/0 at 48x48. Follow-ups noted, not blocking: no config kill-switch for the repair (cheap insurance, [invariant] knob); O(siblings) ~100ms per clean sibling on big merges."}	blake3:wK00vXK0P8AIE4q2oNeUvjFILaafpTolozvoy7kwdDo
1786557703505839	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEygxY		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"DST deep-run evidence (from bn-3gba review, 2026-08-12): at DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48 the production tier reports 4 pre-existing SiblingRefFaithfulness violations (bn-rah2 family, FF-absorb sibling-reset) on seeds 0/15/18 — committed sibling blobs unreachable after a merge. Same FF-absorb sibling family as this bone's root cause (sync_ff_paths_in_worktree global-delta materialization). Retest these seeds after the fix lands; if they persist they are a second defect in the same code region. Default gate budget (16x24) is clean so CI stays green either way."}	blake3:JMZ15w8WeMg057Ff2IApj8HLFbvlhgjs-f8BglAjusU
1786557821915772	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyhBY		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"Lead review of 7405e147 (maw-dev, this session): APPROVED pending merge-time test run (this commit is the other fleet's worker; I lack its just-check evidence, will verify at merge). Verified in source: sync_ff_paths_in_worktree now derives the authoritative set from the sibling's OWN HEAD tree vs target tree (ff_own_stale_paths); ff_paths kept as floor+fallback so read failures only under-report (never regress pre-fix behavior); dirty paths outside the absorbed range are skipped, never clobbered, and WARNED with the maw ws sync fix command; extra refreshes surfaced as NOTE; deletions handled (read_blob_at_path Ok(None) removes, incl. dangling symlinks). Matches the proven mechanism exactly (same approach as sync_target_worktree_to_epoch). Regression test drives the field shape ws_epoch < pre_absorb_epoch < tip, fails unfixed. Interaction check vs bn-3gba: a dirty stale sibling deliberately ends worktree!=HEAD (skipped paths) and bn-3gba's verify skips dirty siblings — consistent, no false repair."}	blake3:Ind0s0Yy8oreoi5lH4ZxxFAmlgruO6M0WUVzUDtnkbQ
1786811455421471	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyhRY		item.create	bn-286g	{"description":"Deep DST (DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48, production tier) fails dst_production_tier_no_work_lost\nwith 4 SiblingRefFaithfulness (bn-rah2) violations on seeds 0, 15, 18: a live sibling\nworkspace's COMMITTED blob becomes unreachable from every ref after a merge op that did not\ntarget that workspace (FF-absorb sibling-reset class). Examples:\nseed=0 step=44 op=merge ws-4 blob f9bb17ed / ws-5 blob 999dbc26;\nseed=15 step=35 ws-6 blob b827ca1c; seed=18 step=32 ws-6 blob fd0387c6.\n\nVerified STILL PRESENT after the bn-p3m9 fix (per-sibling FF materialization delta) landed\nat trunk 1540822c on 2026-08-15 — so this is a SECOND distinct defect in the FF-absorb\nsibling family: a ref-handling bug (sibling branch/epoch ref reset past committed work),\nnot the worktree materialization bug bn-p3m9 fixed.\n\nFirst observed 2026-08-12 during bn-3gba development (pre-existing then, pre-dating all\nfour field-report merges). Default CI budget (16x24) does not reach these seeds, so CI\nstays green; the defect only surfaces at deep budget.\n\nWhere to look: reconcile_epoch_with_branch sibling handling in\ncrates/maw-cli/src/workspace/merge.rs — the paths that move a sibling's branch ref /\nepoch ref (set_head_detached + ref updates) during FF-absorb, for the case where the\nsibling has committed-ahead work. Repro: DST_TRACES=48 DST_STEPS=48 cargo test --test\ndst_production_tier --release --features assurance (seeds 0/15/18).\n\nPrime-Invariant adjacent: committed work orphaned (recoverable only via fsck/unreachable\nuntil gc). Should block the next release tag.\n","kind":"bug","labels":["reliability","dst"],"title":"FF-absorb sibling-reset orphans committed sibling blobs (SiblingRefFaithfulness, deep-DST seeds 0/15/18)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:n2wlGQgiQ5J_GBoktnPRZNtQUV8Qsz--NRM9lc-VMFE
1786811463977835	maw-dev	itc:v3:AWKTmSTM_JOSSTQAAAAAQa7Vbfq6qsAAAAEyhhY		item.comment	bn-p3m9	{"body":"FIXED and shipped to main: 5f73ceb9 (merged first so subsequent merges ran a fixed binary). End-to-end verification: deterministic repro_ffabsorb.sh vs the installed fixed binary reports NO HIT (victim clean; was poisoned on pre.13). NOTE: deep-DST seeds 0/15/18 SiblingRefFaithfulness violations PERSIST post-fix — that is a second distinct FF-absorb defect (ref handling, not materialization), now tracked as bn-286g (urgent)."}	blake3:PtdVWMfx5ivzliIhq-lhOcfHKVso4afL2K5ZmQWkI9c
